For example, the date 'January 1, 2023' would be represented as '01-JAN-2023' in the FND\_STANDARD\_DATE format.

It is important to note that the FND\_STANDARD\_DATE format is a system-wide setting in Oracle EBS, and it can be changed by the system administrator if necessary. However, it is generally recommended to use the default format to ensure consistency and compatibility with other parts of the system."}

